ud6.4:33.1 starts: With regard to these things
ud6.4:33.2 starts: some contemplatives & brahmans.
ud6.4:33.3 starts: They quarrel & fight–
ud6.4:33.4 starts: people seeing one side.
ud6.5:24.1 starts: With regard to these things
ud6.5:24.2 starts: some contemplatives & brahmans.
ud6.5:24.3 starts: Not reaching the footing,
ud6.5:24.4 starts: they sink in mid-stream.
ud6.6:24.1 starts: People are intent on the idea of
ud6.6:24.2 starts: and attached to the idea of
ud6.6:24.3 starts: Some don’t realize this,
ud6.6:24.4 starts: nor do they see it as an arrow.
ud7.6:4.1 starts: For someone with no root, no soil,
ud7.6:4.2 starts: –how creepers?
ud7.6:4.3 starts: Who’s fit to criticize him?–
ud7.6:4.4 starts: the enlightened one freed
ud7.6:4.5 starts: Even devas praise him.
ud7.6:4.6 starts: Even by Brahmā he’s praised.
ud7.7:3.1 starts: One who
ud7.7:3.2 starts: who has gone beyond
ud7.7:3.3 starts: The world, even with its devas,
ud7.7:3.4 starts: he, going about without craving,
ud8.5:9.1 starts: After he had eaten the pig-delicacy,
ud8.5:9.2 starts: a fierce sickness arose in the Teacher.
ud8.5:9.3 starts: After being purged of it,
ud8.5:9.4 starts: “To the city of Kusinarā
ud8.5:16.1 starts: The awakened one,
ud8.5:16.2 starts: with its pristine, pleasing water, clear–
ud8.5:16.3 starts: the Teacher, seeming very tired,
ud8.5:16.4 starts: the Tathāgata, unequalled in the world
ud8.8:8.1 starts: And thus blissful & sorrowless
ud8.8:8.2 starts: are those for whom nothing
ud8.8:8.3 starts: So one who aspires
ud8.8:8.4 starts: shouldn’t make anything
